# Line endings are content here, not a preference.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on this machine rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, and
# drizzle hashes migration files BYTE FOR BYTE into drizzle.__drizzle_migrations
# (migrator.js: sha256 over the file text). So the same migration checked out on
# Windows and on a Linux CI box hashes differently, and `git checkout` of a file
# the local database already applied is enough to change its hash without
# changing a single statement.
#
# That is not theoretical: it made the amended-migration guard in migrate.ts
# report a false positive the first time it ran, on a file restored by git with
# no content change at all.
#
# So migrations and the SQL/JSON around them are pinned to LF everywhere.
*.sql text eol=lf
**/migrations/**/*.json text eol=lf

# Everything else: normalize in the repo, let git decide in the working tree.
* text=auto
